// expect: refuse E_TypeMismatch
// An arm's value is the install's value: an arm that does not resume
// answers the install, so what it answers must be what the install's body
// answers. Here the body answers an Int and the arm a String. On boot
// cf8a6d50 the program compiled clean and ran (exit 0): the handler's type
// carried its effect's instance and not its answer, so no install ever met
// the answer its arms were judged under. The refusal names the arm: `Int vs
// List(Byte) — ~> pipe → at 15:13-15:27: inferred from the arm bail of
// handler h` (the frontier's where leg holds the text).
effect Bail {
  bail() -> Int
}

handler h {
  bail() => "not a number",
}

fn main() = (bail() + 1) ~> h
